WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.371
On the federal side, automated account
management calls for the workflow

2
00:00:04.371 --> 00:00:06.071
definitions, their versions,

3
00:00:06.071 --> 00:00:09.825
and run history exported before
Entra's thirty-day view drops it.

4
00:00:09.825 --> 00:00:13.484
Authenticator management requires
that the first authenticator

5
00:00:13.484 --> 00:00:16.163
is time-limited and goes
to an accountable person.

6
00:00:16.163 --> 00:00:20.551
So the ISSO keeps the pass
policy and the task's settings.

7
00:00:20.551 --> 00:00:23.238
To validate, one kit
check flags hires whose

8
00:00:23.238 --> 00:00:26.225
start date has passed with
no processing record.

9
00:00:26.225 --> 00:00:31.337
Another confirms execution limits are set,
and counts workflows against the ceiling.

10
00:00:31.337 --> 00:00:35.487
Add the run history for the last group
of hires, and the readiness rate.

11
00:00:35.487 --> 00:00:40.575
Lifecycle Workflows and entitlement
management are available in Azure Government.

12
00:00:40.575 --> 00:00:45.524
But Microsoft's government table has
no row for the Temporary Access Pass,

13
00:00:45.524 --> 00:00:48.688
so its availability in
GCC High isn't confirmed.

14
00:00:48.688 --> 00:00:52.201
Before Governance is licensed,
the pipeline enables the

15
00:00:52.201 --> 00:00:55.713
account on the hire date and
the help desk issues the pass.

16
00:00:55.713 --> 00:00:58.700
To roll back, disable
the workflow's schedule.
